# demo/latency.sh, three runs, QNX 8.0 on QEMU (KVM, 2 vCPUs) on WSL2, swtpm; 2026-11-27.
# 1 kHz SCHED_FIFO loop (tools/rt-probe), 30 s per row; jitter = |period - 1 ms| in microseconds.
# witnessd and the TPM driver serve attestation at priority 8; the loop runs above it (10) or below it (7).
# QEMU on a laptop: idle rows already show millisecond outliers from the host. Compare rows, not absolutes.

### run 1
1 kHz loop, 30 s per run; witnessd and the TPM driver serve attestation at priority 8
==> loop at priority 10, idle
rt-probe: priority 10, 1000 Hz, 30000 wake-ups: jitter us p50 6 p99 164 p99.9 993 max 2371 mean 21.0; over 1 ms: 2
==> loop at priority 10, attestation flood
rt-probe: priority 10, 1000 Hz, 30000 wake-ups: jitter us p50 12 p99 149 p99.9 712 max 999 mean 22.7; over 1 ms: 0
  load: 682 attestations (21.3/s) from 8 clients
==> loop at priority 7, idle
rt-probe: priority 7, 1000 Hz, 30000 wake-ups: jitter us p50 6 p99 139 p99.9 335 max 3448 mean 15.5; over 1 ms: 1
==> loop at priority 7, attestation flood
rt-probe: priority 7, 1000 Hz, 30000 wake-ups: jitter us p50 16 p99 167 p99.9 999 max 4293 mean 28.3; over 1 ms: 8
  load: 716 attestations (22.4/s) from 8 clients

